title: Regenerating an Importer
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The invoice scanner adds a `currency` field.  Fix the profile in the
editor, test it in the Console, and then:

# Open the [[Studio]].  Under ''Importers made here'', the ''Invoice Importer'' row now says //the profile has changed since; regenerate to pick up the edits//.
# Click ''Regenerate…''.  The generator opens with every setting the importer was made with, and the version already bumped from 0.1.0 to 0.1.1.
# Click ''Generate'', then download.

The recipient drags the new file in.  Because the version is higher,
TiddlyWiki replaces the installed importer; a same-or-lower version
would have been refused, which is why the generator insists on the
bump.  Nothing else changes for them: same page, same two buttons.

If the original profile has been lost -- a different machine, say --
dragging the //pack// into the Studio puts its baked-in profile in the
Console dropdown and the Studio's profile list, marked as shipping
inside that pack.  Edit it there and regenerate; the copy inside the
pack is the source.
